# `nestjs/no-tautological-equality`

When ESLint reports a tautological equality assertion in `*.spec.ts`, follow the repository skill [fix-nestjs-tautological-equality](.cursor/skills/fix-nestjs-tautological-equality/SKILL.md).

**Remember:** a tautological assertion is evidence that the test is not observing the behavior it claims to protect. Do not manufacture a different expected value from the actual.

**Do not:** disable the rule, derive the expected value from the actual, spread/clone/serialize the actual, reimplement the production algorithm to manufacture an expected value, or invent a contract when the intended outcome is unclear.

**Do:** determine the observable behavior the test intended to prove, repair with an independently derived expected outcome, remove only a redundant tautology, or leave the violation and report the ambiguity.
